;; db: bench_tree
;; Same-generation on a random tree.  The recursive rule has 3 joins, and in
;; the version driven by delta-sg the future clause (edge PY Y) has PY bound
;; right after the driver -- a semijoin filter ("does PY have children?")
;; prunes sg-pairs ending at leaves BEFORE the expanding (edge PX X) join.
;; This is the key soundness test for filters under semi-naive recursion.
table (edge int int)
table (sg int int)

rule (edge P X) (edge P Y) --> (sg X Y)
rule (edge PX X) (sg PX PY) (edge PY Y) --> (sg X Y)
